   "evidence": "Lines 513-517: `if h2 : l = 2 then (Units.map ...).comp (H.signIndicatorHom ...) else 1`. The docstring (lines 511-512) says it is trivial at every other index, and the PR description keeps `hl` because index 4 gives the trivial character.",
   "file": "TauCeti/RepresentationTheory/Tensor/Induction/VirtualCharacter.lean",
   "fix": "Define it for any `[H.FiniteIndex]`, with no `l`, as `(Units.map (Int.castRingHom k).toMonoidHom).comp (Equiv.Perm.sign.comp (MulAction.toPermHom G (G \u29f8 H)))`. Prove the on-`H` value 1 (for normal `H`) and the prime-index off-`H` value `(-1)^(l-1)` (via the single `l`-cycle already shown in `tensorIndClassFun_apply_of_notMem_of_index_prime`) as lemmas.",
   "issue": "`primeIndexSignChar` takes a redundant `{l} (hH : H.index = l)` and splits on `l = 2` (`signIndicatorHom` vs the trivial character). This matches the natural sign character of the action on `G \u29f8 H` only at prime index; at index 4 it is wrongly trivial, which is why the off-`H` lemma must keep `hl`.",
   "line": 513
  }
